; levelcreate.eval — the one New Level writer (docs/level-building.md P1), in a
; scratch copy of the demo world (run with -project lb_create).
;
; A new floor must land IN ITS DUNGEON and be stairs-linked to the floor above
; IN THAT DUNGEON — not to whatever the manifest lists before it. The demo's
; manifest is `crypt1 crypt2 eval_arena`, so a crypt3 appended to it has the
; ARENA as its flat-list predecessor: exactly the control the old writer failed.
;
; And a REROLL keeps every stair the level has — the one up AND the one down —
; because their far ends live on floors the reroll must not touch. crypt3 is
; rerolled twice: alone (one stair), then with crypt4 below it (two), the
; second time into a 12x12 map too small for its stairs, which must grow to
; hold them rather than drop them.
logecho on
reset
levels
generate crypt path:6 seed:7 locks:1
generate again seed:8
generate crypt path:6 seed:9 locks:1
levels view crypt3
generate again seed:10 width:12 height:12
levels new crypt
levels
validate
savemap
